<title>CHILE: Chile's CCU registers new ADR offer.</title>
<headline>Chile's CCU registers new ADR offer.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean brewery Compania Cervecerias Unidas said it has registered a public offering of 3.1 million American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) with the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>The ADR offering is equivalent to 15.7 million shares.</p>
<p>The company, Chile's largest beer maker, will also sell 1.2 million shares to local investors at the same time as the ADR placement, said the statement.</p>
<p>Nearly 38 million shares will be also be first offered to existing shareholders, it said.</p>
</text>
